course: dictionary
lesson: 8481
title: Sanction: permission or punishment?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Sanction» can mean official permission, or it can mean a punishment. The words around it give you the clues. Read «sanctions for bad behaviour» in a school rule: bad behaviour tells you a sanction is a punishment.
explain: «Countries... push with sanctions, refusing trade or freezing money to make a government change course.» The clues are refusing trade, freezing money and change course. A sanction here is an action by countries to punish another country and push it to change. Always check: does your meaning still make sense when you put it in the sentence?
explain: Now look for a clue that points the other way. «Without sanction» means without official permission. The word «without» tells you it is not allowed, so sanction must mean permission. Two meanings, one word: the context decides which one you need.
fact: Sanction can be a noun (a sanction) or a verb (to sanction something).
fact: «Sanction» means official permission or approval, or a punishment for breaking a rule.
fact: «Sanctions» are actions by countries to punish another country, such as stopping trade.
fact: «Rewards and sanctions» in a school means the praise and the punishments the school gives.
fact: «To sanction» something means to allow it officially, or (also) to punish it.
exercise: «Countries push with sanctions, refusing trade to make a government change course.» Here, sanctions are | Gifts of food and medicine | A school lunch menu | *Actions by countries to punish another country | Official team names
exercise: In school, «rewards and sanctions» means | Prizes for sport only | Homework and tests | Sports kit and bags | *Praise for good work and punishments for breaking rules
exercise: «The trip went ahead without sanction from the head teacher.» What does without sanction mean? | Without any money | *Without official permission | Very quickly | With a big party
test: «Many countries put sanctions on Russia after 2022.» In this sentence, sanctions are | Local weather reports | *Penalties, such as stopping trade | Gifts to Russian children | Official team uniforms
test: In the phrase «to sanction a plan», what does sanction mean? | *To allow it officially | To find a lost cat | To walk slowly | To cook a meal
exam: «Russia found other buyers for its oil, so the sanctions hurt but did not stop the war.» Why did the sanctions not stop the war? | *Russia found other buyers for its oil | The war ended before the sanctions began | The sanctions were a gift to Russia | Russia had no oil at all
